# Gone: the New York pages this site carried before it was re-pointed at Florida.
#
# The site was built for New York, then converted city by city to Florida. The
# New York pages were deleted with the conversion, so they already answer 404.
# Google has not caught up: over the 30 days to 14 September 2026 these URLs
# still drew 1,605 of the property's 3,816 Search Console impressions, 42% of
# everything, at an average position of 49 and with zero clicks, because there
# is nothing behind them to click through to.
#
# 410 rather than 404 because 410 is the stronger signal and Google drops a
# 410 from the index faster than a 404 it has to keep re-verifying.
#
# 410 rather than a 301 to the Florida equivalent because there is no
# equivalent. Somebody searching for a garage door in Hicksville or Yonkers is
# in New York, and this company does not work in New York. Pointing them at a
# Florida city page helps neither of them, and Google reads an off-topic
# redirect as a soft 404 anyway.
#
# Netlify's matcher ignores trailing slashes, so one line covers /x and /x/.
# The 410 body is the site's own not-found page; the status is what matters.
#
# Slugs taken from sites/ny-garage/src/data/cities.ts and regions.ts at commit
# 24d5914^, the last commit before the Florida conversion. Checked against the
# 52 Florida cities and 7 Florida regions: no slug collides, so nothing live is
# caught by these rules.

